     AQUAL residual: g mu(g/a0) - g^2/(g+a0) = 0
       g/a0= 0.01   g mu - g_N = -8.132e-20
       g/a0= 0.10   g mu - g_N = +3.469e-18
       g/a0= 0.50   g mu - g_N = +0.000e+00
       g/a0= 1.00   g mu - g_N = +0.000e+00
       g/a0=10.00   g mu - g_N = +0.000e+00
C12_AQUAL      lhs=+0.000000000000e+00  rhs=+0.000000000000e+00  rel.res=+0.000e+00  tol=1e-14  PASS   the action's first integral g-u(g) IS AQUAL mu(x)=x/(1+x)

[P2] alpha_1(1 AU): 2r^2/L*^2 = 8.16126060e-14 (measured L*) ;  r^2 K/gamma = 8.16126060e-14 (action)
C13_ALPHA1     lhs=+8.161260603853e-14  rhs=+8.161260603853e-14  rel.res=+0.000e+00  tol=1e-12  PASS   alpha_1(1AU)=2r^2/L*^2=r^2K/gamma; no beta (A54 G6)
     alpha_1 depends on gamma only; the static solution is beta-free (C07-C10),
     so d alpha_1/d beta = 0 for every beta.

====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- TT sector: theta = O(h^2), so beta cannot enter at quadratic order
====================================================================================================

[P3] TT mode diag(h+,-h+,0): det = 1 - A(tt)**2
     theta = (1/2) d_t ln det = A(tt)*Derivative(A(tt), tt)/(A(tt)**2 - 1)
     theta to O(eps^2) = -eps**2*a(tt)*Derivative(a(tt), tt)
     O(eps) coefficient of theta = 0
C14_TTTHETA    lhs=+0.000000000000e+00  rhs=+0.000000000000e+00  rel.res=+0.000e+00  tol=1e-15  PASS   theta vanishes at O(eps) for a TT mode: no volume change at linear order

[P3] quadratic TT action  S = (1/4K)[ (1+0 beta) hdot^2/4 - k^2 h^2/4 ]
     c_T^2 = <(-R3)>/<K^2> = 1
C15_CT2        lhs=+1.000000000000e+00  rhs=+1.000000000000e+00  rel.res=+0.000e+00  tol=1e-14  PASS   c_T^2 = 1 for every beta (GW170817 |c_T-1|<1e-15)
     dS_TT/dbeta = 0
C16_TTBETA     lhs=+0.000000000000e+00  rhs=+0.000000000000e+00  rel.res=+0.000e+00  tol=1e-30  PASS   the O(h^2) TT action has identically zero beta-coefficient

